{"name":"Tierra Del Fuego Sea Green","hex":"#c2ddd3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"del","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Delaware languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The symbol ∇ used to denote the gradient operator.","the symbol ∂, in the context of a partial differential"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/del"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green","wikidata":"Q373787"},{"title":"Tierra del Fuego","blocks":[{"text":"Tierra del Fuego is an archipelago off the southernmost tip of the South American mainland, across the Strait of Magellan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/NASA_Tierra_del_Fuego_image.jpg/330px-NASA_Tierra_del_Fuego_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tierra_del_Fuego","wikidata":"Q82601"},{"title":"Del","blocks":[{"text":"Del, or nabla, is an operator used in mathematics as a vector differential operator, usually represented by ∇. When applied to a function defined on a one-dimensional domain, it denotes the standard derivative of the function as defined in calculus. When applied to a field, it may denote any one of three operations depending on the way it is applied: the gradient or (locally) steepest slope of a scalar field ; the divergence of a vector field; or the curl (rotation) of a vector field."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Del","wikidata":"Q334508"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Green_vintage_buttons.jpg/500px-Green_vintage_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Green_vintage_buttons.jpg/500px-Green_vintage_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreen_vintage_buttons.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg/500px-Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg/500px-Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACommon_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik